##### Migrate and Modernize a Web Application with Google Cloud: Challenge Lab

Step 1: Create the GKE Cluster

gcloud container clusters create cymbal-k8-cluster \
    --zone=us-east1-b \
    --num-nodes=1 \
    --image-type=ubuntu_containerd \
    --machine-type=e2-medium

Initialize the filters file:

./m2c copy default-filters > filters.txt

./m2c copy gcloud \
    -p qwiklabs-gcp-02-50a4ac09f32d \
    -z us-east1-b \
    -n cymbal-web-vm \
    -o cymbal-web-vm-filesystem \
    --filters filters.txt

Step 3: Copy, Analyze, and Generate Container Artifacts

./m2c analyze \
    -s cymbal-web-vm-filesystem \
    -p linux-vm-container \
    -o cymbal-web-vm-analysis-output

Generate the deployment artifacts: 

./m2c generate \
    -i cymbal-web-vm-analysis-output \
    -o cymbal-migration-artifacts

Get GKE cluster credentials:

gcloud container clusters get-credentials cymbal-k8-cluster --zone us-east1-b --project qwiklabs-gcp-02-50a4ac09f32d

Change directory to your artifacts and run Skaffold to build and deploy:

cd cymbal-migration-artifacts
skaffold run -d eu.gcr.io/qwiklabs-gcp-02-50a4ac09f32d

Confirm the external IP of the GKE service:

kubectl get service cymbal-web-service

Task 3: Deploy the Container to Cloud Run

gcloud run deploy cymbal-web-serverless \
    --image=eu.gcr.io/qwiklabs-gcp-02-50a4ac09f32d/linux-system \
    --region=us-east1 \
    --allow-unauthenticated \
    --port=80

If its web page not working 
gcloud run services add-iam-policy-binding cymbal-web-serverless \
    --region=us-east1 \
    --member="allUsers" \
    --role="roles/run.invoker"
